# Commit, Push, And Deploy To Production

- After completing and verifying a user-requested code change, commit the intended changes and push the current branch to its configured remote.
- Open a PR if one does not already exist for the branch, then merge it to the production base branch (`main`) once checks are green (or immediately if the repo reports no required checks).
- Prefer merge commits (`gh pr merge --merge`) and delete the remote feature branch after merge.
- Include the rule file itself when it has changed.
- Never discard, overwrite, or silently include unrelated user changes.
- Do not push or merge known broken or incomplete work; report any verification or Git blocker clearly.
- After a successful production merge, report the PR URL, branch, short commit/merge hash, and deployment status when available.
